  "classification": "COMPLETE_MIXED",
  "classification_rationale": "GOVERNING CLASSIFICATION (revised this sprint per second independent Codex re-audit): COMPLETE_MIXED, not COMPLETE_NEGATIVE. Real thoracic EIS (condition B) does not clearly outperform the ECG+pleth baseline (condition A): A_minus_B_mean=-0.452 (A better on average), but this comparison REVERSES SIGN when subject 9 (an extreme outlier, A_minus_B=-14.88) is excluded via leave-one-out - the aggregate direction for A-vs-B is not stable across the cohort. B is also worse than its own within-subject deranged-EIS control (C_minus_B_mean=-1.293); this comparison remains negative under leave-one-out but SHRINKS SUBSTANTIALLY without subject 9 (see leave_one_subject_out_sensitivity), meaning even the more diagnostic C-vs-B evidence is partly driven by one influential subject rather than being uniformly negative across the cohort. Given real, substantial subject heterogeneity in both key comparisons - not a uniform negative result - COMPLETE_MIXED (equivalently: NEGATIVE_LEANING_HETEROGENEOUS) is the honest classification. B favors A in 9/12 subjects and favors C in 7/12 subjects (i.e. B is the worst of the three for a majority of subjects), but the magnitude and even the sign of the effect is subject-dependent, not a stable cohort-wide negative.",
